Ladybird traps tkill() and sends the signal with a tgkill() on its
own thread group. Gecko does the same: SandboxFilter.cpp traps tkill
with TKillCompatTrap(), which calls tgkill() with getpid(), for
pthread_kill() in Android’s bionic and in musl. Chromium’s
RestrictKillTarget() kills the process for any tkill(), but Chromium
doesn’t support musl. From reading the sources.

Ladybird’s IPC policy allows select() along with pselect6(), poll(),
and ppoll(). Gecko’s SandboxFilter.cpp allows its CASES_FOR_select,
and Chromium’s syscall_sets.cc lists select among the calls it allows
on x86. From reading the sources.
